################################################################################
# Quantus technology layer map: design (LEF/DEF) names -> QRC tech file names.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS
# --------------------
# The QRC deck wired into the .mmmc is a foundry *Assura* deck:
#     /tsmc65pdk/65/CMOS/LP/pdk/Assura/online/1p9m_6X1Z1U/qrcTechFile
# It was compiled by Techgen from the ICT beside it
#     crn65lp_1p09m+alrdl_6x1z1u_typical.ict
# and therefore carries that ICT's layer names -- poly / metal1..metal10 /
# VIA1..VIA9 -- NOT the P&R names. The design side (tech LEF
# PRTF_EDI_N65_9M_6X1Z1U_RDL.24a.tlef) presents M1..M9 / RV / AP.
#
# With no map, Quantus 21.1 logs "EXTGRMP-155: Layer mappings were not
# specified", then EXTGRMP-330 for every LEF layer, then a hard
# "EXTSNZ-127 ... definition cannot be found in the tech file" for each layer
# the DEF actually uses, and aborts (EXTDPW-103 / EXTGRMP-103, exit 2). No SPEF
# is produced. See ASIC/sta/work/qrc_3534228_20260818_00:28:44.log:409,446-500,
# 1037-1117.
#
# Tempus requires this file whenever extract_rc_qrc_cmd_type is `auto` (the
# default): SSV_21.11.000/doc/tempusCUI/extract_rc_Category_Attributes.html,
# attribute extract_rc_lef_tech_file_map -- "In this mode, the
# extract_rc_lef_tech_file_map attribute is required to be specified."
# Format and the -technology_layer_map spelling come from that page and from
# QUANTUS_21.11.000/doc/quantusUser/Running_Quantus.html.
#
# HOW EACH PAIR WAS ESTABLISHED (topology, not guesswork)
# -------------------------------------------------------
# The ICT states each via's top_layer/bottom_layer, which pins the stack
# ordering uniquely against the tech LEF's ROUTING/CUT sequence:
#   ICT  VIA1 metal1->metal2 ... VIA8 metal8->metal9, VIA9 metal9->metal10
#   LEF  M1 VIA1 M2 VIA2 ... M8 VIA8 M9 RV AP
# so M1..M9 -> metal1..metal9, RV -> VIA9, AP -> metal10. The AP pairing is
# additionally stated outright in the ICT header:
#   "( metal10 is Al-RDL = AP )"
# and corroborated by geometry: ICT metal10 min_width 3 / thickness 1.45 is the
# AlRDL, and ICT metal9 thickness 3.4 is the 1U ultra-thick M9 of this stack.
#
# NW, PW, PO are MASTERSLICE in the tech LEF and CO is a CUT layer; none of the
# four is referenced by any VIA definition in the tech LEF, nor by any macro LEF
# in the design (checked across every *.lef in the routed libs/lef directory).
# They carry no parasitics here. MASTERSLICE layers unused by the DEF are mapped
# to the reserved ICT layer `none` per Running_Quantus.html. CO is deliberately
# left UNMAPPED: the same page guarantees an unused CUT layer yields a warning,
# not an error, and the ICT offers two candidate contacts (polyCont poly->metal1
# and odCont S/D->metal1) that the evidence does NOT disambiguate. If a future
# run raises EXTSNZ-127 on CO, that means CO became load-bearing and the choice
# must be settled from the design, not guessed here.
#
# WHAT THIS FILE DOES *NOT* FIX -- READ BEFORE TREATING ANY SPEF AS SIGNOFF
# -------------------------------------------------------------------------
# This map corrects a NAMING mismatch only. The deck itself is still the TYPICAL
# ICT applied to all three RC corners (best/typical/worst all point at the one
# qrcTechFile). Parasitics produced with this map are single-corner physics
# wearing three corner names. The corner-specific packs under
# CMOS/util/T-N65-CL-SP-036-V1_11a/ do NOT fix this: they are the 6X2Y stack,
# not 6X1Z1U (their ICT gives metal8 0.2/0.5 and metal9 0.2/0.5 against this
# stack's 0.4/0.9 and 2/3.4), so wiring them per corner would replace a
# corner error with a much larger geometry error on the top metals.
################################################################################

extraction_setup \
    -technology_layer_map \
        M1   metal1  \
        M2   metal2  \
        M3   metal3  \
        M4   metal4  \
        M5   metal5  \
        M6   metal6  \
        M7   metal7  \
        M8   metal8  \
        M9   metal9  \
        AP   metal10 \
        VIA1 VIA1    \
        VIA2 VIA2    \
        VIA3 VIA3    \
        VIA4 VIA4    \
        VIA5 VIA5    \
        VIA6 VIA6    \
        VIA7 VIA7    \
        VIA8 VIA8    \
        RV   VIA9    \
        NW   none    \
        PW   none    \
        PO   none
